  "id": "transderm-scop",
  "term": "Transderm-Scop",
  "definition": "Transderm-Scop refers to scopolamine, a plant-derived tropane alkaloid with anticholinergic effects that blocks acetylcholine activity at muscarinic receptors. It is used for effects such as preventing vomiting and reducing vertigo, and it can also decrease secretions and slow gut movement.",
